A Models: A Talk-and-Tweak Human-in-the-Loop Approach  * September 2025\n\n# Dual-Actor Fine-Tuning of VLA Models: A Talk-and-Tweak Human-in-the-Loop Approach\n\n  * September 2025\n\nDOI:10.48550/arXiv.2509.13774\n\nAuthors:\n\nPiaopiao Jin\n\nPiaopiao Jin\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nQi Wang\n\nQi Wang\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nGuokang Sun\n\nGuokang Sun\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nZiwen Cai\n\nZiwen Cai\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nShow all 6 authors Hide\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nRequest file PDF\n\nTo read the file of this research, you can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nPreprints and early-stage research may not have been peer reviewed yet.\n\n## Abstract\n\nVision-language-action (VLA) models demonstrate strong generalization in robotic manipulation but face challenges in complex, real-world tasks. While supervised fine-tuning with demonstrations is constrained by data quality, reinforcement learning (RL) offers a promising alternative. We propose a human-in-the-loop dual-actor fine-tuning framework grounded in RL. The framework integrates a primary actor for robust multi-task performance with a refinement actor for latent-space adaptation. Beyond standard physical interventions, we introduce a lightweight talk-and-tweak scheme that converts human corrections into semantically grounded language commands, thereby generating a new dataset for policy learning. In real-world multi-task experiments, our approach achieves 100% success across three tasks within 101 minutes of online fine-tuning. For long-horizon tasks, it sustains a 50% success rate over 12 consecutive operations. Furthermore, the framework scales effectively to multi-robot training, achieving up to a 2 times improvement in efficiency when using dual robots. The experiment videos are available at https://sites.google.com/view/hil-daft/.\n\n## No file available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the file of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nRequest file PDF\n\n## Citations (0)\n\n## References (26)\n\nResearchGate has not been able to resolve any citations for this publication.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEDITS: Enhancing Dataset Distillation with Implicit Textual Semantics (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/395582916_EDITS_Enhancing_Dataset_Distillation_with_Implicit_Textual_Semantics)\nciteturn8640search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; DOI:10.48550/arXiv.2509.13858 ... In this paper, we propose EDITS, a novel framework that exploits the implicit textual semantics within the image data to achieve enhanced distillation.\n\n# EDITS: Enhancing Dataset Distillation with Implicit Textual Semantics\n\n  * September 2025\n\nDOI:10.48550/arXiv.2509.13858\n\nAuthors:\n\nQianxin Xia\n\nQianxin Xia\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nJiawei Du\n\nJiawei Du\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nGuoming Lu\n\nGuoming Lu\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nZhiyong Shu\n\nZhiyong Shu\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nShow all 5 authors Hide\n\n## Abstract\n\nDataset distillation aims to synthesize a compact dataset from the original large-scale one, enabling highly efficient learning while preserving competitive model performance. However, traditional techniques primarily capture low-level visual features, neglecting the high-level semantic and structural information inherent in images. In this paper, we propose EDITS, a novel framework that exploits the implicit textual semantics within the image data to achieve enhanced distillation. First, external texts generated by a Vision Language Model (VLM) are fused with image features through a Global Semantic Query module, forming the prior clustered buffer. Local Semantic Awareness then selects representative samples from the buffer to construct image and text prototypes, with the latter produced by guiding a Large Language Model (LLM) with meticulously crafted prompt. Ultimately, Dual Prototype Guidance strategy generates the final synthetic dataset through a diffusion model. Extensive experiments confirm the effectiveness of our method.Source code is available in: https://github.com/einsteinxia/EDITS.\n\n## Citations (0)\n\n## References (21)\n\nResearchGate has not been able to resolve any citations for this publication.\n\nDo computer vision foundation models learn the low-level characteristics of the human visual system?\n\nConference Paper\n\n  * Jun 2025--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEDITS: Enhancing Dataset Distillation with Implicit Textual... (https://arxivlens.com/paperview/details/edits-enhancing-dataset-distillation-with-implicit-textual-semantics-2178-ebc94dc0)\nciteturn8640search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; EDITS introduces a novel Dual-Prototype Guidance framework that combines image and text prototypes for synthetic dataset generation. ... Paper ID: 2509.13858\n\nBack ArXiv cs.CV EDITS: Enhancing Dataset Distillation with Implicit Textual Semantics\n\nArXiv cs.CV\n\n# EDITS: Enhancing Dataset Distillation with Implicit Textual Semantics\n\nGuoming Lu, Jiawei Du, Jielei Wang, Qianxin Xia, Zhiyong Shu\n\n2509.13858 Published Sep 17, 2025\n\nChat with paper Cite 中文 View PDF Share\n\n### Publication\n\nPublished: Sep 17, 2025\n\nCategories: cs.CV\n\n### Metrics\n\nSource: ArXiv\n\n## Quick Answers\n\n### What methodology did the authors use?\n\nThe paper proposes EDITS, a framework that enhances dataset distillation by integrating implicit textual semantics. It uses a Vision Language Model (VLM) to generate text descriptions for images, fuses these with image features via a Global Semantic Query module, selects representative samples through Local Semantic Awareness, and generates synthetic datasets using a diffusion model guided by dual prototypes. More in Methodology →\n\n### What are the key results?\n\nEDITS outperforms existing state-of-the-art methods by 1%-3% on high-resolution datasets like ImageNet subsets. — The method achieves superior performance on low-resolution datasets such as CIFAR-10 and CIFAR-100, surpassing VLCP. More in Key Results →\n\n### Why is this work significant?\n\nThis research addresses the limitations of traditional dataset distillation methods that neglect high-level semantic information. By leveraging implicit textual semantics, EDITS enables more accurate and interpretable synthetic dataset generation, which can improve model training efficiency and performance. More in Significance →\n\n### What are the main limitations?\n\nThe method relies on external text generation from VLMs, which may introduce biases or inaccuracies in the textual descriptions. — The approach requires significant computational resources due to the use of large models like CLIP and diffusion models. More in Limitations →\n\n### Paper Preview\n\n### Abstract\n\nDataset distillation aims to synthesize a compact dataset from the original large-scale one, enabling highly efficient learning while preserving competitive model performance. However, traditional techniques primarily capture low-level visual features, neglecting the high-level semantic and structural information inherent in images. In this paper, we propose EDITS, a novel framework that exploits the implicit textual semantics within the image data to achieve enhanced distillation. First, external texts generated by a Vision Language Model (VLM) are fused with image features through a Global Semantic Query module, forming the prior clustered buffer. Local Semantic Awareness then selects representative samples from the buffer to construct image and text prototypes, with the latter produced by guiding a Large Language Model (LLM) with meticulously crafted prompt. Ultimately, Dual Prototype Guidance strategy generates the final synthetic dataset through a diffusion model. Extensive experiments confirm the effectiveness of our method.Source code is available in: https://github.com/einsteinxia/EDITS.\n\n## Key Findings, in focus\n\nSeven facets of this paper, analysed and brought into focus by AI.\n\nAI-generated · verify against source Generated Sep 20, 2025\n\nIn focus · one-line synthesis\n\nThis research addresses the limitations of traditional dataset distillation methods that neglect high-level semantic information.\n\n01\n\nMethodology How they did it\n\nThe paper proposes EDITS, a framework that enhances dataset distillation by integrating implicit textual semantics. It uses a Vision Language Model (VLM) to generate text descriptions for images, fuses these with image features via a Global Semantic Query module, selects representative samples through Local Semantic Awareness, and generates synthetic datasets using a diffusion model guided by dual prototypes.\n\nCopy\n\n02\n\nResults What they found\n\n  * EDITS outperforms existing state-of-the-art methods by 1%-3% on high-resolution datasets like ImageNet subsets.\n  * The method achieves superior performance on low-resolution datasets such as CIFAR-10 and CIFAR-100, surpassing VLCP.\n  * Ablation studies confirm the effectiveness of each component, with combined modules achieving up to a 4.2% improvement on ResNet-18.\n\nCopy\n\n03\n\nSignificance Why it matters\n\nThis research addresses the limitations of traditional dataset distillation methods that neglect high-level semantic information. By leveraging implicit textual semantics, EDITS enables more accurate and interpretable synthetic dataset generation, which can improve model training efficiency and performance.\n\nCopy\n\n04\n\nTechnical Contributions What's new technically\n\nEDITS introduces a novel Dual-Prototype Guidance framework that combines image and text prototypes for synthetic dataset generation. It also incorporates Global Semantic Query and Local Semantic Awareness modules to enhance semantic representation during distillation.\n\nCopy\n\n05\n\nNovelty What sets it apart\n\nThe novelty lies in the integration of implicit textual semantics from VLM-generated descriptions with image features, along with the dual-prototype guidance strategy for generating more semantically rich and diverse synthetic datasets.\n\nCopy\n\n06\n\nLimitations What to be cautious about\n\n  * The method relies on external text generation from VLMs, which may introduce biases or inaccuracies in the textual descriptions.\n  * The approach requires significant computational resources due to the use of large models like CLIP and diffusion models.\n\nCopy\n\n07\n\nFuture Work Where it goes next\n\n  * Scaling EDITS to larger and more complex datasets to improve generalization.\n  * Improving efficiency in low-resource settings by optimizing the framework.\n  * Extending the framework to multi-modal applications such as medical imaging and autonomous driving.\n\n### Paper Details\n\nPaper ID: 2509.13858\n\nCategories:\n\ncs.CV\n\nView on arXiv Download PDF\n\n### How to Cite This Paper\n\n[Button: BibTeX] [Button: APA] [Button: MLA] [Button: Chicago] [Button: IEEE]\n\nReference manager: RIS EndNote\n\n### Authors\n\nGL Guoming Lu 8 papers JD Jiawei Du 19 papers JW Jielei Wang 7 papers QX Qianxin Xia 3 papers ZS Zhiyong Shu 2 papers--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nZiwen Cai (https://www.csauthors.net/ziwen-cai/)\nciteturn8640search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Dual-Actor Fine-Tuning of VLA Models: A Talk-and-Tweak Human-in-the-Loop Approach. ... CoRR, September, 2025\n\n# Ziwen Cai\n\nOrcid: 0000-0003-0317-52